<header class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-inner">
        <div class="eyebrow">Legal &amp; data protection</div>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p>How EduCore collects, uses, shares, retains, and protects personal data across our web platform, Android application, APIs, and support services.</p>
    </div>
</header>

<main class="container legal-layout">
    <aside class="toc" aria-label="Privacy policy contents">
        <strong>On this page</strong>
        <a href="#scope">Scope and roles</a><a href="#data">Data we process</a><a href="#sources">How we obtain data</a>
        <a href="#purposes">Purposes and lawful bases</a><a href="#rbac">RBAC and school separation</a>
        <a href="#sharing">Sharing and disclosure</a><a href="#children">Children and sensitive data</a>
        <a href="#retention">Retention and deletion</a><a href="#transfers">International transfers</a>
        <a href="#security">Security and breaches</a><a href="#rights">Your rights</a><a href="#contact">Contact and complaints</a>
    </aside>

    <article class="content">
        <div class="meta">
            <div class="meta-card"><span>Effective and last updated</span><strong>July 28, 2026</strong></div>
            <div class="meta-card"><span>Privacy contact</span><a href="mailto:support@educoreng.online?subject=Privacy%20Request">support@educoreng.online</a></div>
        </div>

        <p>EduCore Education Technology (“EduCore”, “we”, “our”, or “us”) provides a multi-tenant school-management platform through <a href="https://educoreng.online">educoreng.online</a>, school web portals, the EduCore Android application, application programming interfaces (“APIs”), and related support services (together, the “Service”).</p>
        <p>This Privacy Policy explains how personal data is collected, used, disclosed, retained, and protected when schools, staff, students, parents or guardians, applicants, agents, and platform administrators use the Service. It is intended to reflect the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 (“NDP Act”), the Nigeria Data Protection Act General Application and Implementation Directive 2025 (“GAID 2025”), and other applicable Nigerian laws.</p>

        <div class="notice">
            <p><strong>Important role distinction:</strong> A subscribing school generally determines why and how its school records are processed and is the data controller for those records. EduCore generally processes those records for the school as its technology service provider. EduCore acts as a controller for data collected directly for platform registration, billing, security, support, agent management, and service administration.</p>
        </div>

        <h2 id="scope">1. Scope and Who This Policy Covers</h2>
        <p>This Policy applies to visitors to our public website and users of the web and Android Service, including platform super administrators, school administrators, principals, teachers, other staff, accountants, admission officers, transport officers, health officers, students, parents or guardians, applicants, and registered agents.</p>
        <p>Each school remains responsible for its own privacy notices, the accuracy and lawfulness of data entered by its users, assigning appropriate roles, and responding to requests concerning school-controlled records. Where a school’s notice conflicts with this Policy regarding the school’s own processing purposes, the school’s notice governs those purposes.</p>

        <h2 id="data">2. Personal Data We Process</h2>
        <div class="table-wrap">
            <table>
                <tr><th>Category</th><th>Examples</th><th>Why it is used</th></tr>
                <tr><td>School and platform registration</td><td>School name, address, contacts, logo, domain or portal details, subscription, active-student count, agent or referral information</td><td>Onboarding, tenant configuration, capacity, billing, support, and platform administration</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Identity, account, and RBAC data</td><td>Name, email, phone, staff or student ID, username, hashed password, role, permissions, account status, profile or passport photograph</td><td>Authentication, identity cards, role-based access, account recovery, and security</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Student, applicant, and guardian records</td><td>Biographical details, date of birth, gender, address, nationality, admission documents, class, guardian relationship and contacts, transfer and alumni records</td><td>Admissions, enrolment, student administration, safeguarding, and parent access</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Academic and conduct records</td><td>Subjects, classes, attendance, timetable, lesson plans, assessments, scores, CBT responses, results, report cards, remarks, skills, discipline, certificates, and transcripts</td><td>Teaching, assessment, reporting, promotion, and academic administration</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Staff, attendance, and HR records</td><td>Employment details, attendance times, leave, qualifications, salary settings, bank details, payroll items, payslips, pension and deductions</td><td>Staff administration, attendance, payroll preparation, and reporting</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Fees and payment records</td><td>Fee structures, bills, invoices, discounts, payment references, amounts, status, receipts, expenses, and settlement information</td><td>School billing, parent payments, reconciliation, and financial reports</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Health and transport records</td><td>Allergies, medical conditions, medication, health visits, emergency notes, routes, vehicles, drivers, manifests, stops, and student transport assignments</td><td>Restricted school health support, safety, and transport administration</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Communications</td><td>Announcements, messages, notifications, email or SMS delivery details, reminders, contact forms, and support correspondence</td><td>School communication, service notifications, and support</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Technical and security data</td><td>IP address, device and operating-system information, app version, API tokens, session data, authentication and audit logs, error and diagnostic information</td><td>Service delivery, fraud prevention, troubleshooting, audit, and security</td></tr>
            </table>
        </div>

        <h3>2.1 Mobile permissions, location, camera, and photographs</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Location:</strong> When a school enables staff-attendance geo-fencing, the Android app may request device location at clock-in or clock-out to determine whether the attendance event is within the school’s permitted radius. Location is not required for unrelated app functions.</li>
            <li><strong>Camera and QR:</strong> The app may use the camera to scan attendance or identity QR codes. QR scan values and attendance events may be transmitted to the Service for verification.</li>
            <li><strong>Attendance photographs:</strong> An authorised proxy clock-in flow may capture and store a live photograph as attendance evidence.</li>
            <li><strong>Profile photographs and documents:</strong> Users may upload passport photographs, admission documents, and other authorised school records. The app requests permission when access is needed.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>2.2 Cookies and similar technologies</h3>
        <p>Our web Service uses necessary cookies and local storage for login sessions, security, preferences, and core functionality. We may use limited diagnostics to understand errors and performance. We do not use student records for behavioural advertising.</p>

        <h2 id="sources">3. How We Obtain Personal Data</h2>
        <p>We receive personal data directly from users; from schools and their authorised administrators; from parents, guardians, staff, students, and applicants; from the Android app and connected devices when permissions are used; from payment, messaging, or email providers; and from technical logs generated when the Service is accessed.</p>

        <h2 id="purposes">4. Purposes and Lawful Bases</h2>
        <p>Depending on the relationship and data involved, processing may be based on performance of a contract, steps requested before a contract, consent, compliance with a legal obligation, protection of vital interests, performance of a task in the public interest where applicable, or legitimate interests that are not overridden by data-subject rights.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Service delivery:</strong> Operate admissions, records, academics, exams, attendance, fees, payroll, staff HR, health, transport, communications, reporting, agents, and platform administration.</li>
            <li><strong>Authentication and RBAC:</strong> Confirm identity, issue and manage accounts, restrict modules and records by role, and enforce tenant separation.</li>
            <li><strong>Payments and subscriptions:</strong> Generate bills, process and reconcile payments, calculate school subscriptions, and maintain transaction evidence.</li>
            <li><strong>Safety and safeguarding:</strong> Support authorised health, emergency, attendance, and transport processes.</li>
            <li><strong>Communication and support:</strong> Deliver notices, reminders, password-reset messages, announcements, and responses to enquiries.</li>
            <li><strong>Security and improvement:</strong> Detect misuse, investigate incidents, maintain audit logs, diagnose faults, and improve reliability and usability.</li>
            <li><strong>Legal compliance:</strong> Meet lawful requests and accounting, data-protection, dispute, and regulatory obligations.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="rbac">5. Role-Based Access and School Separation</h2>
        <p>EduCore is designed as a multi-tenant platform. School records are associated with the relevant school, and access is controlled through authentication, tenant checks, and role-based access control (“RBAC”). For example, teachers receive assignment-based academic access, parents receive access to linked children, accountants receive finance and payroll access without teacher-only attendance or score-entry permissions, and health records are restricted to authorised health or administrative personnel.</p>
        <p>School administrators are responsible for assigning, reviewing, and removing user roles promptly. No access-control system is infallible, and users must report suspected unauthorised access immediately.</p>

        <h2 id="sharing">6. Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
        <p>We do not sell personal data. We may disclose only what is reasonably necessary to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>The relevant school and authorised users:</strong> According to their role, assigned responsibilities, and linked records.</li>
            <li><strong>Parents or guardians:</strong> For children linked to their verified parent or guardian account.</li>
            <li><strong>Service providers:</strong> Hosting, backup, security, payment-processing, banking or settlement, email, SMS, support, and diagnostic providers operating under appropriate instructions or obligations. Payment providers may include Monnify, Paystack, or Flutterwave where selected or enabled.</li>
            <li><strong>Professional advisers:</strong> Auditors, legal advisers, insurers, or consultants where confidentiality obligations apply.</li>
            <li><strong>Authorities or legal claim participants:</strong> Where disclosure is required by applicable law, lawful process, regulatory request, safety needs, or the establishment, exercise, or defence of legal claims.</li>
            <li><strong>A successor organisation:</strong> In a merger, financing, reorganisation, or transfer of the Service, subject to appropriate notice and protection.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Payment-card or bank-channel credentials entered on a payment provider’s page are handled under that provider’s privacy terms. EduCore normally receives the payment reference, amount, status, and reconciliation details rather than full card credentials.</p>

        <h2 id="children">7. Children and Sensitive Personal Data</h2>
        <p>The Service is built for schools and therefore processes children’s personal data. Schools must provide appropriate notices and obtain parental, guardian, or other lawful authorisation where required. Children should use the Service only through accounts issued or authorised by their school.</p>
        <p>Health information, payroll and bank information, precise attendance location, photographs, and certain identity or safeguarding records may require heightened protection. We limit these records to the relevant purpose and authorised roles and expect schools to apply data minimisation and confidentiality controls. We do not use children’s school records or sensitive personal data for advertising.</p>

        <h2 id="retention">8. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
        <p>Retention depends on the type of record, the school’s instructions, the duration of the account, operational need, dispute or security requirements, and applicable legal obligations:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>School records are normally retained while the school account is active and as required for authorised school administration.</li>
            <li>Financial, payroll, audit, security, and transaction records may be retained for applicable statutory, accounting, fraud-prevention, or dispute periods.</li>
            <li>Backups are protected and overwritten through the applicable backup cycle; deletion from active systems may not immediately remove a record from an existing protected backup.</li>
            <li>When deletion is approved, data is deleted, de-identified, or placed beyond normal use unless continued retention is legally required or necessary to protect a claim.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Individual school users should first request correction, access, or deletion from their school administrator because the school controls most educational and employment records. A school administrator may contact EduCore for a school-level export or deletion request. We verify identity and authority before acting.</p>

        <h2 id="transfers">9. International Transfers</h2>
        <p>Some hosting, messaging, security, support, or payment providers may process data outside Nigeria. Where personal data is transferred internationally, we use or require a lawful transfer basis and appropriate protection consistent with Part VIII of the NDP Act and GAID 2025, such as an adequacy basis, approved transfer instrument, contractual protection, consent where valid, or another permitted condition.</p>

        <h2 id="security">10. Security and Personal-Data Breaches</h2>
        <p>Measures used to protect the Service include encrypted network transmission, password hashing, authenticated API access, RBAC, tenant-aware authorisation, audit logging, restricted health workspaces, access revocation, backups, and security monitoring. Security also depends on schools and users protecting credentials, devices, roles, and exported records.</p>
        <p>No internet service can guarantee absolute security. If we become aware of a personal-data breach, we will investigate, contain, document, and provide notifications to the affected school, data subjects, or the Nigeria Data Protection Commission where required by applicable law.</p>

        <h2 id="rights">11. Your Data-Protection Rights</h2>
        <div class="table-wrap">
            <table>
                <tr><th>Right</th><th>What it means</th></tr>
                <tr><td>Be informed</td><td>Receive clear information about the processing of your personal data.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Access</td><td>Ask whether personal data is being processed and request a copy, subject to lawful limits.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Rectification</td><td>Ask for inaccurate or incomplete personal data to be corrected.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Erasure or restriction</td><td>Request deletion or restricted processing where the legal conditions apply.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Object</td><td>Object to processing based on certain lawful bases or direct marketing.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Data portability</td><td>Request eligible data in a structured, commonly used, machine-readable format.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Withdraw consent</td><td>Withdraw consent for future processing where consent is the lawful basis.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Automated decisions</td><td>Request appropriate safeguards and human review where a qualifying solely automated decision has a legal or similarly significant effect.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Complain</td><td>Raise a complaint with the relevant school, EduCore, or the Nigeria Data Protection Commission.</td></tr>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p>Submit an EduCore privacy request to <a href="mailto:support@educoreng.online?subject=Privacy%20Request">support@educoreng.online</a> with the subject “Privacy Request”. For school-controlled records, we may refer the request to the relevant school. We may request information needed to verify identity, authority, and the account or school involved. We aim to respond without undue delay and within the period required by applicable law.</p>

        <h2>12. Third-Party Services and Links</h2>
        <p>The Service may link to payment processors, school websites, or other third-party services. Their privacy practices are governed by their own notices. Schools are responsible for integrations they choose to configure and for ensuring that users receive any additional required information.</p>

        <h2>13. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this Policy to reflect platform, provider, legal, or security changes. The current version will be published at this route with a revised “Last Updated” date. Where a change materially affects users, we may also notify school administrators by email or display a notice in the Service.</p>

        <h2 id="contact">14. Contact and Complaints</h2>
        <div class="contact-card">
            <p><strong>EduCore Education Technology</strong><br>Privacy and Support Desk<br>Lagos, Lagos State, Federal Republic of Nigeria</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@educoreng.online?subject=Privacy%20Request">support@educoreng.online</a></li>
                <li><strong>Telephone:</strong> <a href="tel:+2347065595768">07065595768</a></li>
                <li><strong>WhatsApp:</strong> <a href="https://wa.me/2347065595768" target="_blank" rel="noopener">+2347065595768</a></li>
                <li><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://educoreng.online">https://educoreng.online</a></li>
            </ul>
            <p>If you are not satisfied with our response, you may lodge a complaint with the <a href="https://ndpc.gov.ng" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nigeria Data Protection Commission</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </article>
</main>

